      "id": 1,
      "text": "East Harwich’s early economy thrived on the sea, shifting from whaling to cod fishing after oil was discovered.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.usacitiesonline.com/macountyeastharwich.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits at 41°42′28″N 70°1′53″W, a precise spot on Cape Cod’s eastern shore.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Harwich%2C_Massachusetts"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "East Harwich covers roughly 21.4 square miles of land, a modest stretch of Cape Cod coastline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.usacitiesonline.com/macountyeastharwich.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Water bodies account for about 1.82 square kilometers of the area, adding to its maritime charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.usacitiesonline.com/macountyeastharwich.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Its latitude places it 41.70 degrees north of the equator, while its longitude is 70.03 degrees west of the prime meridian.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.usacitiesonline.com/macountyeastharwich.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town’s elevation is 69 feet above sea level, keeping it safely above typical coastal tides.",
